Z||000015||Dave Gunsul||12-20-2001||11:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LoW_KeY:<BR>[B<P>how high could I take the compression on the 3.4? 10/1? <P>pretty much every machine shop is like "oooh oooh I'm not sure"<P>clue me in guys   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>-KC[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've got custom forged Ross pistons in my V6 with 10:1 compression. You should be able to<BR>go to 11:1 with no hitting depending on how big your cam is. I found this info out just after I had my short block done otherwise I would have gone with 11:1 myself. The Ross pistons are a little more expensive at $92.00 a piston but my machine shop friend just couldn't say enough good things about them so it would profit you to look into them. With custom pistons you can prett much go with whatever compression you want it's just a matter of making sure the clearence is okay. A company like ross will make whatever you want you just need the engine specs and a good machine shop that deals with them.<P><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>Activities Director<BR>Northern IL. Fiero Enthusiasts<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
